{
    "_comment": "Patronage & Great Works (src/systems/patronage.js). Clients (artists, scholars, architects, physicians, chroniclers) are offered in a town's salon, chosen by a hash of the world seed, the town and the month (no RNG). They draw a weekly stipend, produce works on commission and can be poached by rival Houses or leave when unpaid or idle. Great Works are multi-stage projects at a settlement the player rules or holds a house in: each stage wants goods + gold delivered, then days of paid labour. Every effect key has a reader: research (Technology.getResearchBonus), conversion (PlayerReligion.conversionMultiplier), education (Upbringing growth), vision (Player.updateVisibility), festivalRenown (Festivals.getReputation), riverCross (Infrastructure.getRiverPenalty), care/woundHeal (Ailments), mood (Taxation happiness target via settlement.patronage), monthlyPrestige (House Prestige, paid by Patronage). Kingdoms build wonders too (npc*), first to finish a unique work claims it for the world.",
